-- title:
--   Rigidity of unramified henselian local algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0$ be a commutative local ring, $W_0$ a commutative henselian local ring equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure whose structure map $A_0 \to W_0$ is a local homomorphism, and assume $W_0$ is unramified over $A_0$ in the sense that $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$ equals the ideal of $W_0$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_{A_0}$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_{W_0} = \mathfrak m_{A_0}\,W_0$; assume further that the residue field extension $\operatorname{ResidueField}(W_0)/\operatorname{ResidueField}(A_0)$ is finite-dimensional and separable. Let $C$ be a commutative local ring that is Hausdorff for its $\mathfrak m_C$-adic filtration, that is, $\bigcap_{N} \mathfrak m_C^{N} = 0$. Let $u_1, u_2 \colon W_0 \to C$ be ring homomorphisms with $u_1$ local, and suppose that $u_1$ and $u_2$ agree after precomposition with the structure map $A_0 \to W_0$, and that $u_1(w) - u_2(w) \in \mathfrak m_C$ for every $w \in W_0$. Then $u_1 = u_2$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the lifting property for an unramified (formally étale) henselian local algebra with finite separable residue extension, in the form needed when the target is merely separated for its adic topology rather than complete. It is used in the construction of an isomorphism between an adic completion and a quotient of a power series ring over the coefficient ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_ringHom_eq_of_forall_sub_mem_maximalIdeal_of_maximalIdeal_eq_map_of_isSeparable.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
